// Example 06: failures.
//
// How code says that something went wrong. Application code says what
// failed; the compiler and runtime decide how that is shown to whoever
// called. There is no `throw`, no exception and no error code chosen by
// hand: a failure is a declared type, every callable lists the failures
// that can leave it, and every call that can fail says at the call site
// what happens when it does.
//
// The project takes cake orders. README.md lists the files in reading
// order.
application {}
